{{!-- The overlay the bar collapses into below the nav breakpoint (1200px).

It carries exactly what the bar sheds: search, the whole menu, and the call to action. It starts
underneath the bar rather than at the top of the viewport, and the bar's height is measured rather
than assumed — the reading bar is shorter than the listing bar, and a hardcoded offset would leave a
strip of the wrong Surface showing on one of them. `siteMenu` measures on boot, on every open, and on
a resize while it is open, so a rotation cannot leave the offset stale either.

The search control is a button dressed as a field, not a field. There is nothing for a field to
submit to: Ghost owns search, and its popup has an input of its own, so a real input here would ask a
visitor to type their query twice. It carries `data-ghost-search`, so it is also the trigger that
keeps the platform's ⌘K shortcut alive on Surfaces whose bar has no visible search control — see the
note in chrome/header.hbs.

It is the one control here that does **not** close the panel. A visitor who reached search from the
panel should land back on the panel when they dismiss it, which is also what makes the focus restore
in main.js land on something visible; closing underneath the popup would return them to a page they
did not ask for and drop the scroll lock while a full-screen popup is still up.

This whole element is in the DOM at every viewport width; `nav:hidden` is what keeps it out of a wide
layout. `x-cloak` covers the moment before Alpine boots. --}}
<div
	id="site-menu"
	x-show="menuOpen"
	x-cloak
	x-bind:style="'top:' + barH + 'px'"
	x-on:keydown.escape.window="close()"
	class="bg-bg nav:hidden fixed inset-x-0 bottom-0 z-40 overflow-y-auto">
	<div class="container py-8">
		<button
			type="button"
			data-ghost-search
			class="border-border bg-surface font-ui text-muted flex w-full cursor-pointer items-center gap-2.5 rounded-sm border px-3.5 py-3 text-left text-base">
			<span
				aria-hidden="true"
				class="font-mono">⌕</span>
			{{t "Search posts"}}
		</button>

		<nav
			aria-label="{{t "Main navigation"}}"
			class="mt-8 flex flex-col gap-2.5">{{navigation variant="overlay"}}</nav>

		{{> "chrome/cta" class="btn btn-primary font-ui mt-9 block rounded-sm px-[18px] py-3.5 text-center text-base font-semibold no-underline"}}
	</div>
</div>
